WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.609 --> 00:00:07.830
Let's talk about those tens of millions of
dollars that Donald Trump raised after the

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:16.980
election and before January 6th meant to fight
voter fraud in the courts and met to support

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.740
the Republican incumbent senators in Georgia,
both of whom lost.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.570
Donald Trump spent none of that money on the
things he claimed he was raising the money

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.570
for.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.080
And of course, anybody who looked at the fine
print as we did would have predicted exactly

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:40.410
this 76 million dollars Donald Trump raised
for what ultimately was a slush fund, claiming

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.070
I need the money to challenge the results
of the election.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.480
I need the money to make court filings.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.000
I need the money to help Republicans win in
Georgia so that Republicans maintain control

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.440
of the Senate.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.260
But through the end of twenty twenty, not
a dime was spent on those causes.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.870
Maybe we don't yet have reporting for Q1 spending.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.440
Maybe in those first five days of January,
Trump spent some of the seventy six million

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.080
on the things he promised to spend it on.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.370
I doubt it.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:16.060
He, a Republican familiar with the fundraising
fundraising operation, said, quote, He put

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.360
nothing back.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:18.880
He didn't care.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.420
He put all this money in the bank for his
own legal fights.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.450
He never cared about Georgia's races.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:29.960
But not only that, he didn't even spend the
money on vote challenges.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:35.620
And if you recall, back when Trump was doing
this, we showed you the fine print, which

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:42.510
said, depending on which fundraising scheme
we were talking about, 50 percent or even

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:50.200
more of every dollar raised could go towards
the Trump campaign general fund to pay off

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.210
Trump's campaign debt.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.210
He said it.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:58.520
I mean, listen, he said it in a deceptive
way in the fine print, sort of like a software

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.960
end user agreement that's 30 pages long that
nobody reads.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:02.960
Right?

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.360
I mean, but he did do it and we were reporting
it.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:11.580
And it was reported so completely predictable
that this is exactly what was going to happen.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.550
Jason Miller was asked what what happened,
Jason?

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.970
Where did the money go?

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.239
And Jason Miller so far has not responded
for comment.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:26.230
Now, the truth is, Trump may well need this
money for his own legal defense.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:31.020
And I think it's absolutely disgusting that
he's taking advantage of his own supporters,

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.580
who he clearly never cared about his people.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:40.069
But ultimately, it's scammers and more scammers
and more scammers taking advantage of people

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:45.780
who are often scammers in their own ways,
people who were delighted to be bamboozled

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:51.400
by Trump in 2016 and wanted to continue believing
that Trump was somehow going to figure out

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.810
something even though he lost the election.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:54.810
This was.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:03:00.540
These were the perfect marks to be bamboozled
in this way, and ultimately the money is going

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.880
to the Save America Leadership Committee of
Trump.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.239
This is nothing more than a slush fund where
the money can be used for just about anything

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:10.239
Trump wants.

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:14.900
If Trump wants to pay himself a salary out
of this money, he could do it.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:20.330
And it is unbelievable that these folks fell
for it hook, line and sinker, despite the

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:24.540
fact that we were widely reporting that this
is exactly what was going on.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:31.430
Now, when you say these people fell victims
to a scam and we should feel bad for them.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.470
I don't know about that.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:39.140
You know, it is these folks who say we don't
need a nanny state government.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:43.519
We don't need the government protecting everybody
from everything all the time.

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:44.519
These are adults.

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:49.989
In the end, these are adults who presumably
voted for Trump in 2016 and or 2020.

00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:54.170
These are adults who, despite the fact that
there was no evidence, they fell for the idea

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.910
that Trump actually won and Joe Biden didn't.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:57.910
They fell for it.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.330
I mean, look at look at everything that they
believed at some point.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:04.660
Do they have any responsibility themselves
to figure out what's true?

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:09.860
They fell for the lie that donating to Trump
might actually change the results of an election,

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:13.220
even though the election everything was happening
on schedule.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:17.829
There were they said, oh, December 14th is
going to be delayed and it wasn't.

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:22.289
And then December, what was, you know, January
six was going to be delayed.

00:04:22.289 --> 00:04:25.469
And the riots delayed it by a couple of hours
and it wasn't.

00:04:25.469 --> 00:04:28.729
And then the inauguration is not going and
it did.

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:30.069
They fell for it all.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:35.460
Do they really deserve now to be bailed out
from the fact that they were scammed?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:40.020
Not according to their own political philosophy,
which is no nanny state government, none of

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.020
this stuff.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:44.720
So everybody but his cult knew this would
happen.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:51.599
They are it's hard to even call them suckers
because they were so willing.

00:04:51.599 --> 00:04:54.009
I don't want to call it Stockholm Syndrome.

00:04:54.009 --> 00:05:00.369
I don't know what to call it, but they I have
a hard time now feeling as though they need

00:05:00.369 --> 00:05:06.569
to be bailed out in some way because Trump
put it at the bottom of the emails.

00:05:06.569 --> 00:05:07.749
It's how Trump governed.

00:05:07.749 --> 00:05:12.090
This was the administration, the scam administration
from day one.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:16.059
And these people got exactly what they voted
for, which is Trump ending up with I believe

00:05:16.059 --> 00:05:17.409
it's the seventy six million.

00:05:17.409 --> 00:05:22.180
I think it's 45 million in some kind of joint
fundraising account and then the other thirty

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:28.810
one million in that Defend America, Save America
thing that Trump himself controls.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:32.160
So, you know, Trump is going to do fine financially.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.160
Very clearly.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.759
A lot of those folks who donated money that
they probably couldn't even really afford

00:05:37.759 --> 00:05:42.869
to donate may now have serious financial troubles,
but they have only Trump and their own ignorance

00:05:42.869 --> 00:05:44.069
to thank for that.

00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:50.110
Later, by the way, we will talk about other
other scams that continue to fester related

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.419
to this administration.

00:05:51.419 --> 00:05:55.439
But the question I have for you, I want to
hear from you on Twitter where you can find

00:05:55.439 --> 00:05:57.469
me at Pakman.

00:05:57.469 --> 00:06:02.080
Should we feel bad for these people who were
swindled by Trump's fundraising to the point

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.169
that somebody should bail them out?

00:06:04.169 --> 00:06:05.919
I believe the answer is no.

00:06:05.919 --> 00:06:07.999
I'm willing to hear other ideas.

00:06:07.999 --> 00:06:53.709
Find me on Twitter 

00:06:53.709 --> 00:07:20.400
at David Pakman,

